"Kent Paul Dolan" <xanthian@well.com> writes:
> In vanilla, my Dwarven Valkerie, about to decend from the Oracle
> hears:
> 
>     You hear snoring snakes.
> 
> _What_!???!

A reference to the oracle of Aesculapius at Epidaurus, where sacred
snakes roamed freely in the dormitories in which pilgrims slept, and
were supposed to be the agents causing dreams diagnosing the latter's
illnesses (as interpreted by the priests). Other oracular sounds are
"You hear a strange wind." (referring to the oracle of Zeus at Dodona)
and "You hear convulsive ravings." (referring to the oracle of Apollo
at Delphi). There's also a couple of sounds you hear when
hallucinating that refer to the Usenet Oracle.

